  "sourceFindings": [
    "All sixteen complete selected Arabic paragraphs at 515–530 remain byte-for-byte unchanged from the pinned source. The batch adds 41 complete English segments, six complete chapters and one separately browseable Arabic chapter quotation. All previous 514 entry objects and eight other active book packs remain unchanged.",
    "Historical print PDF pages 145–148 and modern print PDF pages 140–143 were visually inspected. The downloaded full PDF hashes match the existing pinned witnesses. Bewley 515–530 and pinned Khan-family 1.10.515–1.10.530 were individually compared; English comparison bodies are not copied into the app.",
    "515 retains both repeated invitations, kneeling, silence and the complete wall statement. 516 preserves the selected we, first third then half then or-a-third, narrator forgetfulness and the Muadh/Shubah closing transmission omitted from one English comparison. Counted units after sixty to a hundred remain implicit.",
    "517 preserves the full name clarification and related-to-me chain. 518 preserves seven-before-eight, the selected prayer order, singular rainy-night suggestion and unnamed final speaker; the comparisons’ added Anas name is not imported.",
    "519–521 remain separate reports with their own pronouns, chains and closing wording. Abu Usamah’s phrase remains after 520 as selected, although the modern print places it with the chapter heading. All four closing transmitters at 521 remain. Ibn Hajar’s lexical discussion is cited separately; working sunlight/shade wording remains provisional.",
    "522 retains the narrator’s forgetfulness, prayer-name alternatives and morning ending. 523–526 retain their separate destinations and chains; the historical print reverses the al-Awali/Quba order, so reports are matched individually. No travel-time or metric-distance inference is inserted.",
    "527 does not import intentionally from an English gloss; the historical-only closing lexical remark is documented without insertion. 528 retains the cloudy-day expedition and singular collective work, without adding all/good or a legal explanation.",
    "529 retains the full-moon clarification, exact selected Quranic fragment and Ismail’s final remark. The chosen light-mim sense is explicitly provisional and linked to Ibn Hajar’s account of the alternative readings. 530 preserves the selected reporting verb, unnamed questioner, pronouns and leaving-before-coming order."
  ],
